 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Government websites in four countries just switched themselves off.",
   "s": 0.125,
   "e": 3.415,
   "words": [
    0,
    8
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody hacked them.",
   "s": 3.695,
   "e": 4.525,
   "words": [
    9,
    11
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "They were fixing a security bug in PHP, the programming language behind WordPress and about 7 out of 10 websites.",
   "s": 4.95,
   "e": 11.26,
   "words": [
    12,
    31
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Fixing a bug like that takes two steps.",
   "s": 11.7,
   "e": 13.8,
   "words": [
    32,
    39
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "First, you find it.",
   "s": 14.055,
   "e": 15.025,
   "words": [
    40,
    43
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, you fix it everywhere.",
   "s": 15.355,
   "e": 16.865,
   "words": [
    44,
    48
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "You'd think finding it is the hard part, right?",
   "s": 17.38,
   "e": 19.97,
   "words": [
    49,
    57
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And for 14 years, nobody did.",
   "s": 20.535,
   "e": 23.135,
   "words": [
    58,
    63
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, in August, two security teams using AI tools found it and quietly told the people who make PHP so a fix could be ready before anyone else knew.",
   "s": 23.905,
   "e": 32.52,
   "words": [
    64,
    92
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Except, the details of the bug leaked online hours before the fix came out.",
   "s": 33.08,
   "e": 38.21,
   "words": [
    93,
    106
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Cloudflare, which protects a big chunk of the web, says it saw tens of thousands of break-in attempts in 45 minutes, and millions by evening.",
   "s": 38.85,
   "e": 47.07,
   "words": [
    107,
    131
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody knows yet how many got in.",
   "s": 47.635,
   "e": 49.255,
   "words": [
    132,
    138
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So now comes step two, the slow one.",
   "s": 49.815,
   "e": 52.135,
   "words": [
    139,
    146
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Someone has to install that fix on every site, and there are about 22 million copies of PHP out there that could be hit.",
   "s": 52.655,
   "e": 59.515,
   "words": [
    147,
    170
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If a site can't update fast enough, the safest thing is to switch it off until it can.",
   "s": 60.075,
   "e": 64.51,
   "words": [
    171,
    188
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "That's what those government sites did.",
   "s": 65.065,
   "e": 66.405,
   "words": [
    189,
    194
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And one in three sites on PHP runs a version so old that the people who make PHP don't fix it anymore.",
   "s": 67.0,
   "e": 73.11,
   "words": [
    195,
    216
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "For those, it's switch off or hope the hosting company sorts it out.",
   "s": 73.515,
   "e": 77.56,
   "words": [
    217,
    229
   ]
  }
 ],
